{
  "title": "Vroeger",
  "goal": "Describe past states and familiar childhood routines with the simple past of zijn, hebben, and a few common verbs.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Vroeger",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "id": "7931b52d-90a7-4608-a73c-78a805e5c25e"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Thursday 7 January 2027. Sofia and Noor talk about growing up in Valencia and Groningen. In this lesson you will describe past states and familiar routines with the simple past. Verbs are blue, time expressions orange, and the new past forms are bold.",
      "id": "7953a653-a03a-4c55-94ef-d3fc45b15996"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Story: childhood memories",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "id": "acef16c7-459b-49c7-953a-411cd30372df"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Sofia, waar woonde je als kind?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ik woonde in Valencia, in een rustige straat."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Ik woonde in Groningen, vlak bij mijn school."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Had je een step?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Ja, ik had een rode step. En jij?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ik had een blauwe step."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Wat deed je na school?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ik speelde vaak buiten met vriendinnen."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "3cae05f8-db7d-4efd-9ed0-4bbbc3aee4e7"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "vroeger",
              "meaning": "in the past; when someone was younger",
              "example": "Vroeger woonde ik in Valencia.",
              "id": "d80cf566-d0e1-41c8-b808-51e8545892f7"
            },
            {
              "term": "als kind",
              "meaning": "as a child",
              "example": "Als kind woonde Noor in Groningen.",
              "id": "4fc4e532-1880-497f-9506-9f02fba9058f"
            },
            {
              "term": "de basisschool",
              "meaning": "primary school",
              "forms": "de basisscholen",
              "example": "Mijn basisschool was vlak bij huis.",
              "id": "72c96cdc-7511-4032-93e2-afdcf225c777"
            },
            {
              "term": "de speelplaats",
              "meaning": "school playground",
              "forms": "de speelplaatsen",
              "example": "Op de speelplaats speelde ik vaak.",
              "id": "5cf99cbb-2dd3-4bac-82a3-db3676a1d85f"
            },
            {
              "term": "de step",
              "meaning": "scooter (kick scooter)",
              "forms": "de steps",
              "example": "Noor had een rode step.",
              "id": "b9ea1f2b-53db-4d70-91b4-3cab0cc0c92e"
            },
            {
              "term": "na school",
              "meaning": "after school",
              "example": "Na school speelde ik buiten.",
              "id": "017d2114-bc4b-444b-be43-10eeb9e3e358"
            },
            {
              "term": "buiten spelen",
              "meaning": "to play outside",
              "example": "Sofia speelde vaak buiten.",
              "id": "418eaaa6-622c-4301-8e41-7851101a033e"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "70cc171b-96b4-4413-a85d-bad682229dad"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "26f71b13-35de-48dd-871f-faed5519e582"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "The simple past",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "id": "9f3e40c5-64e8-4063-a8ec-45bb30ca6165"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Use these forms to talk about a past state or situation. For a regular verb, add -te/-ten or -de/-den to the stem. The last sound of the stem decides which ending you use.",
      "id": "340b9673-e989-4733-b03f-abdc193f5bc5"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": "zijn: ik was, jij was, hij/zij was; wij/jullie/zij waren. hebben: ik had, jij had, hij/zij had; wij/jullie/zij hadden.",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "id": "97b468ca-3fb5-4836-b778-ecd5bed37111"
    },
    {
      "type": "columnList",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "Singular",
              "id": "ad9066bf-ed60-41a8-a535-af28d088e01d"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "ik was / had",
              "id": "10419807-1533-49ee-acae-278ec919a430"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "jij was / had",
              "id": "13e3923d-204f-43c2-8f12-feb29e9a547e"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "Sofia was / had",
              "id": "168ee5ac-5e55-4bbc-b676-f7fe7b7f133e"
            }
          ],
          "id": "1f15bff5-acae-4a41-a3ac-b7c5701d9802"
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "Plural",
              "id": "5606e41c-961f-480a-a2c2-4be4e6962369"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "wij waren / hadden",
              "id": "c6962358-aa18-4324-903a-4c021025ce82"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "jullie waren / hadden",
              "id": "b1f7a418-492b-444c-bf5d-21354e29ec07"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "Noor en Sofia waren / hadden",
              "id": "fae952ad-5de8-4788-9ddd-1f14e173a85e"
            }
          ],
          "id": "c8b51d33-78b2-416b-a413-819032a26df9"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b74f9999-b6e0-4597-9af3-cd726adcedf9"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Vroeger ",
        {
          "text": "was",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " Sofia vaak thuis."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia was often at home as a child.",
        "note": "was is the simple past of zijn."
      },
      "id": "c718c992-7629-4fea-a15a-cc8f355f6d82"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Noor ",
        {
          "text": "had",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " een rode step."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Noor had a red scooter.",
        "note": "had is the simple past of hebben."
      },
      "id": "9d061da3-3995-48c1-a7c2-5625737d1955"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": "The ending also shows singular or plural: ik woonde, wij woonden.",
      "props": {
        "variant": "important",
        "icon": "star"
      },
      "id": "3ee86de3-cc62-45cd-8769-945acbed5bc4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A stem ending in a sound from ’t kofschip takes -te/-ten. Other final sounds take -de/-den. Add the ending to the verb stem: woon → woonde; fiets → fietste.",
      "id": "0eaaad57-5dbc-4fc9-b93b-8458b9c4a549"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": "The -te ending starts with a clear t; -de starts with d. Keep the stem spelling: fiets + te = fietste.",
      "props": {
        "variant": "pronunciation",
        "icon": "volume-2"
      },
      "id": "e4bcbfaa-76b5-4dae-b34d-d0f3431d310a"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": [
        "Do not use a present form for a finished past situation: ",
        {
          "text": "ik woon",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true,
            "backgroundColor": "gray"
          }
        },
        " → ",
        {
          "text": "ik woonde",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "icon": "triangle-alert"
      },
      "id": "08913ce9-a6f1-4ddf-952b-930cdb4cae7a"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "A few familiar verbs",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "id": "2a483680-c98f-4c52-a9f9-3761dd568828"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "Regular verbs",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "wonen → woonde / woonden",
          "id": "4a955dd5-4b92-4c5b-80b9-2a2beb4e3d63"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "fietsen → fietste / fietsten",
          "id": "97311be8-f766-412d-9bde-bf85982d5dc3"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "spelen → speelde / speelden",
          "id": "b52720bf-c36e-40e6-bcc5-e2b6f67d3be9"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "werken → werkte / werkten",
          "id": "e85a6cb6-3a9b-4020-b4ba-bd84fe497ce6"
        }
      ],
      "id": "96f81b6a-34aa-48b2-a0d6-1f0fad334952"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "Learn these common forms as individual words",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "gaan → ging / gingen",
          "id": "84ff4313-4fcf-48fc-be2e-2417e172f20e"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "komen → kwam / kwamen",
          "id": "ec85cb4b-7d36-41c4-ab62-32287b13a150"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "doen → deed / deden",
          "id": "4016a7f7-e83e-4fce-860a-6ab03d940d2a"
        }
      ],
      "id": "386755bc-7ac7-40ab-aa45-deb384c6f078"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": "The short strong forms are common: ik ging, ik kwam, ik deed. Learn each pair as a set.",
      "props": {
        "variant": "hint",
        "icon": "lightbulb"
      },
      "id": "2689ec5b-db86-4601-890f-21fd8d182970"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Noor ",
        {
          "text": "fietste",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " vaak naar school."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Noor often cycled to school.",
        "note": "The stem fiets ends in s, so the past ending is -te."
      },
      "id": "a4e3e990-70fb-45f8-b709-c10b1d69f8a5"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Sofia ",
        {
          "text": "speelde",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " na school buiten."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia played outside after school.",
        "note": "The stem speel ends in l, so the past ending is -de."
      },
      "id": "c1c9f2c3-3d7c-48cc-b52f-924306b1c978"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Wij ",
        {
          "text": "woonden",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " in Groningen."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "We lived in Groningen.",
        "note": "Plural subject wij takes -den."
      },
      "id": "b448daee-437b-4408-92d3-e8f17856d49c"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Mijn school ",
        {
          "text": "was",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " klein."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "My school was small.",
        "note": "was is a past form of zijn."
      },
      "id": "66aa1c98-3cdd-4a45-b05f-c030916b0b1c"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Ik ",
        {
          "text": "had",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " een blauwe step."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "I had a blue scooter.",
        "note": "had is a past form of hebben."
      },
      "id": "2098441a-9b3c-4dd3-988f-67051b5fe8d9"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Noor ",
        {
          "text": "ging",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " vaak naar de speelplaats."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Noor often went to the playground.",
        "note": "ging is learned as an individual strong form."
      },
      "id": "08687c72-a841-4faf-999a-b3f237e68c23"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Soms ",
        {
          "text": "kwam",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " Sofia lopend naar huis."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sometimes Sofia came home on foot.",
        "note": "kwam is singular; lopend is familiar vocabulary."
      },
      "id": "d34b7f5c-c71d-413c-b2ce-1f4c95467cbe"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Na school ",
        {
          "text": "deed",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " Noor haar huiswerk."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "After school Noor did her homework.",
        "note": "deed is learned as an individual strong form."
      },
      "id": "abececde-9d67-447f-87bd-7f811c4ab844"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "ac7bd098-aeeb-4a36-8079-e3f0e82e3389"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Story: a school afternoon",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "id": "fee2ee1c-068e-41bc-a413-e4fedaab86f2"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Was je school klein?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Ja, mijn school was klein. En jouw school?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Mijn school was ook klein."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Fietste je naar school?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Nee, ik ging meestal lopend. Mijn school was dichtbij."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Wat deed je na school?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ik speelde buiten of ik fietste naar de speelplaats."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Ik ging soms naar de speelplaats."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "0ef35c3d-e71a-4d6a-a588-44f05b3f8574"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "wonen",
              "meaning": "to live; past forms",
              "forms": "woont · woonde · gewoond",
              "example": "Vroeger woonde Noor in Groningen.",
              "note": "The simple past woonde/woonden is the new focus; the participle is a reference form from Part V, row 25.",
              "id": "d328ebc6-22f4-4dc4-b346-91e1b35d0c14"
            },
            {
              "term": "fietsen",
              "meaning": "to cycle; past forms",
              "forms": "fietst · fietste · gefietst",
              "example": "Noor fietste naar school.",
              "note": "The simple past fietste/fietsten is new; the participle is reference data.",
              "id": "f3affecd-1893-4374-ae63-272688b41c3e"
            },
            {
              "term": "spelen",
              "meaning": "to play; past forms",
              "forms": "speelt · speelde · gespeeld",
              "example": "Sofia speelde vaak buiten.",
              "note": "The simple past speelde/speelden is new; the participle is reference data.",
              "id": "7783f5bf-b136-4a26-b98f-83cc940824c2"
            },
            {
              "term": "gaan",
              "meaning": "to go; past forms",
              "forms": "gaat · ging · gegaan",
              "example": "Noor ging naar de speelplaats.",
              "note": "The simple past ging/gingen is introduced as a fixed common form; participle known from Part V, row 26.",
              "id": "26fab668-af56-42fc-abc8-7f9f73ce3fed"
            },
            {
              "term": "komen",
              "meaning": "to come; past forms",
              "forms": "komt · kwam · gekomen",
              "example": "Sofia kwam lopend naar huis.",
              "note": "The simple past kwam/kwamen is introduced as a fixed common form; participle known from Part V, row 26.",
              "id": "f10ec397-3a1f-4b77-8863-d859a0840a28"
            },
            {
              "term": "doen",
              "meaning": "to do; past forms",
              "forms": "doet · deed · gedaan",
              "example": "Wat deed Noor na school?",
              "note": "The simple past deed/deden is introduced as a fixed common form; participle known from Part V, row 27.",
              "id": "8b215010-dac0-4b66-afdf-bcd8fbeb1134"
            },
            {
              "term": "het huiswerk",
              "meaning": "homework",
              "example": "Noor deed haar huiswerk.",
              "id": "d0092142-9b3c-4290-8cbc-0de772c0a458"
            },
            {
              "term": "werken",
              "meaning": "to work; past forms",
              "forms": "werkt · werkte · gewerkt",
              "example": "Ik werkte vroeger vaak.",
              "note": "The simple past werkte/werkten is new; the participle is reference data from Part V, row 25.",
              "id": "edd83739-76ce-4d43-91ef-0c68f1affb03"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "95c388d3-c9dc-419b-b2f2-4b2f864f4a6d"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Remember the patterns",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "id": "4a830f15-8132-4770-8906-98281d86e240"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "Find the subject: one person or more than one?",
      "id": "f1303f43-3f8e-41b6-a8b1-03c411fe335c"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "For zijn and hebben, choose was/waren or had/hadden.",
      "id": "b50ec438-4b32-45d1-82f1-0aea47df9466"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "For a regular verb, choose -te/-ten or -de/-den from the final stem sound.",
      "id": "56bb0a8d-a18f-4835-b4a3-f148e0f5ed37"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "For gaan, komen and doen, learn ging, kwam and deed as fixed forms.",
      "id": "697413b6-787f-4cf6-933d-1bbf4aac4bba"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the examples, the verb is blue and time words are orange.",
      "id": "8858b914-cb62-4eed-a668-e14efbdbc745"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Remember: was/waren, had/hadden, -te/-ten, -de/-den.",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "blue"
      },
      "id": "fb38dbc4-d3e5-46a5-bb78-41b510152636"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "fc1c4a42-a366-4acc-8cab-25e9c6f67a95"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Practice",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "id": "713f9c29-cb5e-4887-87a6-9866793a982f"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Choose was, waren, had or hadden",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "id": "308e7ed2-98a6-40e9-aa0d-4ff99b2235ae"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Fill in the correct past form.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia … acht jaar. (was)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "was"
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor en haar klas … klein. (waren)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "waren"
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Ik … een step. (had)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "had"
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wij … een speelplaats. (hadden)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "hadden"
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Jij … vaak buiten. (was)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "was"
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia en Noor … veel tijd. (hadden)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "hadden"
              ]
            },
            {
